// Lander II - Settings: the player's choices, and where they are kept.
//
// The settings are a small object saved as JSON text in
// Choices:Lander2.Settings (the file <Choices$Write>.Lander2.Settings,
// normally $.!Boot.Choices.Lander2.Settings on the hard disc), so you can
// read or edit them in !Edit. A missing, damaged or out-of-date file just
// gives the defaults for anything that doesn't make sense.
//
// OPTIONS describes every setting for the settings screen: its key, the
// label shown, the allowed values and how each one is shown. An option
// marked enhanced only matters with the Enhanced look, and one marked
// arcade only with the Arcade sound set (the settings screen shades them
// otherwise).

